14. BUSINESS RULES AND DATA INTEGRITY

Implement and test the following rules:

1. One product variant must not have multiple conflicting inventory balances for the same stock location.
2. SKU uniqueness must be enforced.
3. An order must not reserve more stock than is available.
4. Concurrent orders must not cause inventory overselling.
5. Every stock change must have an associated inventory movement.
6. A cancelled order must release its stock reservation when the order lifecycle requires it.
7. Refunds must be reflected in appropriate financial reports.
8. Product cost changes must not silently rewrite historical cost calculations.
9. Every ambassador commission must have a traceable basis.
10. Duplicate order processing must not create duplicate stock movements or commissions.
11. Reference numbers must be unique.
12. Only authorized users may change financial records.
13. An ambassador must only see records within their own permitted scope.
14. An ordinary user must never assign themselves an administrator or ambassador role.
15. Failed operations must not leave partially updated business records.
16. A successful UI message must correspond to a confirmed successful backend operation.

Use database transactions, uniqueness constraints, idempotency mechanisms, or equivalent protections where appropriate.

